    "updated_at": "2023-03-14T02:20:12Z",
    "body": "^I agree with what is being said above, I would have expected it to create the default config first, and then print it\r\n\r\nAnother use case is if you specify a non-existing file in `STARSHIP_CONFIG`, `starship print-config` will panic.\r\n\r\npwsh on windows terminal:\r\n```pwsh\r\n~\r\n❯ $env:STARSHIP_CONFIG = \"nonExistingFile.txt\"\r\n\r\n~\r\n❯ starship print-config\r\nthread 'main' panicked at 'Failed to load starship config', src\\configure.rs:223:5\r\nnote: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace\r\n```\r\n\r\nA friendly message for this case might be:\r\n> The path \"nonExistingFile.txt\" specified in STARSHIP_CONFIG does not exist",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
