    "updated_at": "2023-03-15T11:48:25Z",
    "body": "@Ceres445 I think in any case, `starship print-config` should be always print the config that is used by the prompt.\r\n\r\nI checked these two cases:\r\n* `STARSHIP_CONFIG` pointing to a non-existing file\r\n* Empty `STARSHIP_CONFIG` and no `~/config/starship.toml` existing\r\n\r\nIn both cases, the prompt just uses the default config.\r\nSo `print-config` should just print the default config in these cases, true?",
